### Requests straight to the wallet service, bypassing the gateway: for debugging only.
### X-User-ID stands in for what the gateway would set. Clients use api/gateway.http.
@wallet = http://localhost:8081
@owner = 7d3c5a8e-1111-4222-8333-944455556666
@bob = 0b5e2f1a-2222-4333-8444-a55566667777

### Open a wallet
# @name created
POST {{wallet}}/v1/wallets
X-User-ID: {{owner}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"currency": "USD"}

### Deposit 10.50. Send it twice: the second response is a replay, and the balance grows once.
POST {{wallet}}/v1/wallets/{{created.response.body.id}}/deposits
X-User-ID: {{owner}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: deposit-demo-1

{"amount": 1050, "currency": "USD"}

### Balance
GET {{wallet}}/v1/wallets/{{created.response.body.id}}/balance
X-User-ID: {{owner}}

### Entries, newest first
GET {{wallet}}/v1/wallets/{{created.response.body.id}}/entries?limit=20
X-User-ID: {{owner}}

### A second wallet, for transfers
# @name bob
POST {{wallet}}/v1/wallets
X-User-ID: {{bob}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"currency": "USD"}

### Transfer 3.00 to it
POST {{wallet}}/v1/transfers
X-User-ID: {{owner}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: transfer-demo-1

{"from": "{{created.response.body.id}}", "to": "{{bob.response.body.id}}", "amount": 300, "currency": "USD"}
